// `@generate(Comparable)` walks each field through its own `compareTo`, so every field must have an order. A
// `bool` has none in kama (the prelude gives `Comparable` to the numbers and `string`), and the derive says
// which field stopped it rather than inventing `false < true`.
@generate(Comparable)
type value Switch {
    int32 id;
    bool on;
    public ctor make(int32 id) { this.id = id; this.on = true; }
}

fn int32 main()
{
    Switch a = Switch.make(id: 1);
    Switch b = Switch.make(id: 2);
    return a < b ? 1 : 0;
}
